---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import PersonSchema from '../components/schema/PersonSchema.astro';
import AboutPageSchema from '../components/schema/AboutPageSchema.astro';
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const quickAnswer =
  'Perfume Picks is an iPhone app for keeping track of a fragrance ' +
  'collection, and I build and run it on my own. It files the bottles you ' +
  'own, logs every wear and picks a scent each morning from your own ' +
  'wardrobe. It doesn\'t sell fragrance. It makes money from an optional ' +
  'Pro subscription and retailer affiliate links.';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="I'm Bob Guillow, and I build Perfume Picks on my own. It's an iPhone app for keeping track of a fragrance collection."
  path="/about"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <AboutPageSchema />
    <PersonSchema />
    <BreadcrumbSchema crumbs={[{ name: 'About', url: `${SITE.url}/about` }]} />
  </Fragment>

  <p class="brand">{SITE.name}</p>
  <h1>About Perfume Picks</h1>
  <p class="effective">An iPhone app for a fragrance wardrobe, built and run by one person.</p>

  <QuickAnswer text={quickAnswer} />

  <h2>Who runs Perfume Picks?</h2>
  <p>
    I'm <strong>{SITE.founder.name}</strong>. I build and run Perfume Picks on my
    own, and it's published under {SITE.legalEntity}, my own company. There's no
    outside investor, ad network or parent company, so I make the product and
    privacy decisions myself, and I'm the one who answers
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>
    Perfume Picks is an iPhone app for fragrance collectors. It files your
    wardrobe with a remaining-mL meter and what you paid for each bottle, logs
    every wear with the occasion, the weather and a rating, builds a Fragrance
    DNA profile from the bottles you love and the swipes you make, and picks a
    Scent of the Day from your own wardrobe. A dupe finder shows cheaper
    bottles that smell close, and Perfume Wrapped recaps your year.
  </p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It doesn't sell fragrance. Fragrance pages link to retailers, and I may earn a small commission if you buy through one.</li>
    <li>It isn't a scraper of other fragrance sites. The catalog comes from commercial fragrance-data providers and manual curation.</li>
    <li>It isn't a marketplace, so there are no listings, auctions or decant swaps.</li>
    <li>There are no ads in the app or on this site.</li>
    <li>I don't sell or share your data for advertising. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> has the details.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it makes money</h2>
  <p>
    Perfume Picks is free to download. Pro is $2.99 a month or $24.99 a year,
    with a 7-day free trial. It removes the free limits on the wardrobe, wear
    log, scans and swipes, unlocks the full dupes list and adds Perfume Wrapped.
    Apple handles billing, so payment details never reach my servers.
  </p>
  <p>
    Fragrance pages also have buy links to retailers. If you buy through one, I
    may earn a small commission. It's disclosed on the page and in the
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, and the price you pay is the same.
  </p>

  <h2>Why I built it</h2>
  <p>
    The big fragrance reference sites are built for looking a bottle up, and
    most newer apps are built for shopping. Perfume Picks is for the bottles
    already on the shelf: what you own, what you've worn, and what to wear
    today.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
  <p>
    Articles are written from collecting experience and primary sources like
    manufacturer notes, perfumer interviews and IFRA documentation. Facts link
    to their sources and opinions are labeled. The updated date only changes
    when an article does.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Press, partnerships and feedback all go to
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. I usually
    reply within a day.
  </p>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
